-- @db file
-- 150 tables, each with an index, in a page_size=512 database: the schema
-- table rooted at page 1 becomes a multi-level b-tree (page 1 is then an
-- interior page whose header starts after the 100-byte file header). One
-- CREATE statement is about 3000 bytes long, so its sqlite_schema record
-- overflows. The engine must find every object.
-- @phase sqlite
PRAGMA page_size = 512;
